#---
# purpose: "a lambda named where it is used drives Enum.each through a grounded call, not the boxed seam"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# fz-kdt.155's control. The same `Enum.each/2` shape as
# `mailbox_closure_each.fz`, except the callable is named right here, so the
# each-step callsite carries an exact callee and calls the lambda's own
# executable directly. That grounded call is the one case where the callsite
# DOES own the callee it is narrowing: its discarded result reaches the
# lambda's own return demand, both halves settle on zero delivered lanes, and
# nothing crosses the boxed seam. Widening the boxed convention must leave this
# path exactly as it is.
fn main() do
  double = fn (x) -> dbg(x * 2) end
  Enum.each([1, 2, 3], double)
  dbg(:done)
end
